    description: "Adjacent finding of audit-findings 0021 (Step 5). Filed, not moved.\nelixir.yaml rows Task.async / async_stream / start / start_link / Supervisor.start_child as ipc_send (\"Task spawns -- async execution boundary\"). A spawn inside the BEAM transfers no data across the process boundary at the call; the axiom (ADR-0050 / ADR-0049 ruling 1: \"what data crosses the process boundary at this call site\") does not admit it. The spawned function's own calls are where any crossing happens.\nEffect: each Task spawn is an `ipc` taint sink and an ipc_send headline crossing. Not measured.\nFix shape (not decided): no row, or process_send if the argument closure is considered sent to the new process (erlang's spawn rows are the precedent to check first -- grep erlang.yaml for spawn before deciding)."  # 7973
    fields: {}  # 7973
